From cd6bb4096d93f5c82172589ced1992bbaca6ebf6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex <richardstallman42@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:09:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] feat(compressor): userfaultfd write tracking where
 soft-dirty does not work

arm64 kernels have no CONFIG_MEM_SOFT_DIRTY. smash decided soft-dirty
worked because /proc/self/clear_refs and pagemap opened; the kernel took
the clear as a no-op and bit 55 stayed 0, so every page looked never
written, Phase 3 was skipped, and each tick walked every page table for
nothing. Hot pages were compressed anyway; only Phase B's content check
discarded them.

The write tracker is now chosen once per process by testing it
(selectWriteTracker, SMASH_WRITE_TRACK=auto|softdirty|uffd|none, reported
as track= on the stats line):
- softdirty: probed by writing a scratch page, clearing, and reading the
  bit back (0), then writing again (1);
- uffd: async userfaultfd write-protect (WP_ASYNC + WP_UNPOPULATED,
  Linux 6.7) over the arena, read and re-armed per tick with PAGEMAP_SCAN;
  opened UFFD_USER_MODE_ONLY so unprivileged processes can use it; a
  scratch page is checked end to end first;
- none: files open, nothing works; no per-tick clear/scan work.
SMASH_SOFTDIRTY=0 and unavailable /proc keep selecting Phase 3 PROT_READ.
UAPI constants are defined locally for old build headers.

A MAP_FIXED remap drops the userfaultfd registration (verified in a
prototype), so remapPages re-registers via g_after_remap_track_hook; the
post-fork reset closes the inherited fd so the child selects afresh.

Measured on x86 with bit 55 masked to simulate arm64: auto now picks uffd
and matches real soft-dirty (hot set live; 3-second writer 60 MiB RSS,
10.5 ms per write pass, 8.5 s CPU vs 60 MiB / 10.3 ms / 8.6 s), where the
old behaviour compressed all 8192 hot pages. SMASH_SOFTDIRTY=0 is not a
workaround: PROT_READ monitoring was slowest on both workloads. A forked
child that starts a thread reports track=uffd with its hot set tracked.

New test_uffd_write_tracking: written pages must not compress at any tick,
including one that went through remapPages(). Discriminators: tracker
none -> both compress at tick 1; remap hook removed -> only the remapped
page (tick 2). Suite 53/53 default and forced-uffd, unprivileged and root.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
